<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain leaves its key rate at 6.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain leaves its key rate at 6.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain said on Tuesday it left its key money rate unchanged at six percent at its regular repurchase tender for central bank certificates.</p>
<p>It allotted 3.85 trillion pesetas against 3.86 trillion bid.</p>
<p>The Bank of Spain last cut its key money market rate by 25 basis points to 6.0 percent of January 16.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
